# Security Operations

- Production secrets never live in source control.
- Use a secret-management abstraction for DB, registry, signing and runner credentials.
- Give each runner a distinct authenticated identity; prefer mTLS or equivalent strong service identity.
- Do not expose unauthenticated runtime management APIs.
- Admin/high-impact operations require explicit authorization, auditability and stronger authentication such as MFA.
- Support global lab-disable and runner-drain emergency controls.
- Any runtime/network/gateway/secrets/supply-chain change requires Security Agent review.
